UID:63d21705308184cd@role-business-corporate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261006T000107Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] In-person\, no-excuse absentee voting is unde
 rway in Maine
DESCRIPTION:AUGUSTA\, MAINE\n– Secretary of State Shenna Bellows today t
 raveled to Brunswick Town Hall to mark the start of in-person\, no-excuse 
 absentee voting in Maine today.\n“Maine is always a national leader in v
 oter turnout\, and we saw record turnout in the June primary. In person ab
 sentee voting – Maine’s version of early voting – is part of the spe
 cial sauce that makes voting convenient to the citizenry and drives up tur
 nout\,” said\nSecretary Bellows\n. “Anyone can vote early for any reas
 on starting today until October 29\, and there are lots of ways to vote ab
 sentee – in person\, by mail or utilizing a secure ballot drop box.”\n
 This week\, voters who are not able to make it to the polls on Election Da
 y or who simply wish to avoid the crowds can begin casting absentee ballot
 s\, either in-person at their local town hall or by mailing back their sig
 ned and sealed ballot or dropping it in a local secure ballot box. As of F
 riday\, October 2\, more than 70\,000 Mainers had requested an absentee ba
 llot. Absentee ballot reports are posted on Tuesdays and Thursdays on the 
 Secretary of State’s website.\nBrunswick Town Clerk Fran Smith joined Se
 cretary Bellows to talk about the tasks and challenges that face local ele
 ction officials this election cycle and why Mainers can expect business as
  usual for the November 3 General Election.\n“This is a busy but excitin
 g time for our office\, as I know it is for towns across the state\,”\ns
 aid Brunswick Town Clerk Fran Smith\n. “Our local staff\, as well as vol
 unteers on Election Day\, are so incredibly vital to ensuring everything r
 uns smoothly right up through the counting of the ballots after the polls 
 close on Election Day.”\nAs absentee voting gets underway\, Secretary Be
 llows urged voters to make a plan to ensure their ballots are returned by 
 close of polls on Election Day. In Maine\, only those ballots received by 
 close of polls are counted\, regardless of postmark. Maine offers an onlin
 e absentee ballot tracking service for voters to track the status of t\nht
 tps://www.maine.gov/sos/news/person-no-excuse-absentee-voting-underway-mai
 ne
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/news/person-no-excuse-absentee-voting-underw
 ay-maine
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
