SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: Training for New 
 MaineCare Partner Portal
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare 
 Partner Portal\nAttention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare Par
 tner Portal\nSep 21\, 2026\nWe have\npreviously shared\nthat a refreshed a
 nd upgraded MIHMS\, with a new “MaineCare Partner Portal\,” is coming 
 in October 2026. This will replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal. We
  are now inviting trading partners to\nregister for training that began Se
 ptember 8\, 2026\nto help you prepare for the transition to the new portal
 . Trading partners include providers\, billing agents\, health plans\, cle
 aringhouses\, and business associates. Trading partners have an important 
 role to play in supporting a smooth transition and uninterrupted access to
  the portal after go-live.\nGainwell Technologies will be leading live vir
 tual instructor-led training sessions. These courses will provide the know
 ledge and skills needed to navigate the new portal\, complete daily busine
 ss functions\, and use new portal features. Training demonstrations\, mate
 rials\, and supporting resources will help participants prepare for a succ
 essful transition.\nSteps you need to take to attend training\nReview the 
 available training topics listed below and identify the sessions that alig
 n with your role and responsibilities.\nUse the LMS registration (instruct
 ions below) to create an account\, access the training catalog\, and enrol
 l in applicable sessions.\nContact Gainwell (instructions below) if you ne
 ed assistance.\nRecorded sessions and other training materials will be ava
 ilable in the LMS after training sessions for ongoing reference.\nMaineCar
 e Partner Portal Training Sessions\nCourse Name\nDescription\nME - TPT - M
 igrated Trading Partner Log In and Account Maintenance Training (ILC)\nLea
 rn how to complete first-time login activities\, configure multi-factor au
 thentication (MFA)\, manage user accounts and permissions\, perform accoun
 \nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-tr
 ading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-09-21
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-09-21
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
